            <ArticleTitle>[Related substances in orlistat detected with UPLC-MS/MS].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>380-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The study aims to identify related substances in orlistat pharmaceutical substance from different production technologies. Advanced technologies including UPLC-QTOF-MS and UPLC-QTrap-MS were used and the structures or molecules of 10 kinds of related substances in orlistat were identified. The experimental data were valuable to the quality control and development of orlistat.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
